<header><p class="st-kicker">sultanate · Maritime Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Kasepuhan Sultanate</h1><p class="st-meta">1677 CE – 1815 CE (approx.) · capital Cirebon</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Senior branch of the divided Cirebon Sultanate in West Java, whose palace preserves one of the oldest royal compounds on Java.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panembahan-girilaya">Panembahan Girilaya</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cirebon">Cirebon</a> died as a hostage at the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mataram-sultanate">Mataram</a> court in 1662, his sons were freed in 1677 with help from the rebel <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trunajaya">Trunajaya</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/banten-sultanate">Banten Sultanate</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan-ageng-tirtayasa">Sultan Ageng Tirtayasa</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banten">Banten</a> divided Cirebon among them, making the elder, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pangeran-martawijaya">Pangeran Martawijaya</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Sepuh, the senior sultan, of Kasepuhan.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Kasepuhan held the old Pakungwati palace founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunan-gunung-jati">Sunan Gunung Jati</a>, whose shrine made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cirebon">Cirebon</a> a centre of Javanese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>. The sultan shared Cirebon with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kanoman-sultanate">Kanoman Sultanate</a>, and from 1681 both accepted <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/dutch-east-india-company-territories">Dutch East India Company</a> protection. Court culture blended Javanese, Sundanese, Chinese and Islamic elements, visible in batik and mask dance.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herman-willem-daendels">Herman Willem Daendels</a> and then the British during <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/british-java">British Java</a> stripped the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cirebon">Cirebon</a> sultans of governing power, and by 1815 they had become pensioned nobles. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/keraton-kasepuhan">Keraton Kasepuhan</a> remains the seat of a ceremonial sultan and a major heritage site.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="sultanate, 1677 CE – 1815 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">sultanate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Maritime Southeast Asia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:93.07%;width:2.75%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1677 CE – 1815 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>sultanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Cirebon</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Martawijaya (Sultan Sepuh I)</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Javanese (Cirebon)</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/indonesia">Indonesia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kasepuhan</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1746&amp;focus=kasepuhan-sultanate" aria-label="Kasepuhan Sultanate on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7685 2430 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kasepuhan Sultanate lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M8005 2686L8005 2686M8005 2686L7959 2663"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M8005 2686h0M7959 2663h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8005 2686h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M8005 2686h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Cirebon. <a href="/atlas?year=1746&amp;focus=kasepuhan-sultanate">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
